# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill it in. That file is gitignored, so it
# never reaches GitHub.
#
# `.env.local` is read by scripts/serve.mjs, in the server process. The browser
# never receives it. Do not move these values into src/ or public/ — everything
# there is bundled or served verbatim, so the key would be readable by every
# visitor in the browser's network tab, and GitHub's secret scanning would revoke
# it as soon as it was pushed.
#
# After editing, run: npm start

# Enables the Ask-the-data assistant. Users are then never prompted for a key.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults are fine.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts

# Optional shared-password gate over the whole site, including /api/*.
# Leave blank on a trusted office LAN; set it before exposing the port anywhere else.
# BEMMP_PASSWORD=
# BEMMP_USER=cyrix
